      "description": "Watch Crystal Palace vs Manchester City highlights and goals from Premier League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 28, 2026. The Premier League stage was set at Selhurst Park on August 28, 2026, as Crystal Palace hosted Manchester City . Both teams entered the fray looking to secure vital points in what promised to be an intense tactical battle. City Take Charge Early Manchester City established their dominance from the opening whistle, controlling the tempo and pinning Crystal Palace back. An early scare for the hosts came in the 7th minute when Erling Haaland saw his goal-bound effort hacked off the line. The pressure finally told in the 17th minute; Josko Gvardiol initiated a move that saw Antoine Semenyo provide a pinpoint cross for Erling Haaland to head home. Despite several more attempts and a yellow card for Rayan Cherki , the visitors headed into the break with a slender but deserved lead. A Frenetic Second Half The match exploded into life after the interval. In the 54th minute, Rayan Cherki doubled the lead with a sharp left-footed finish, assisted by Phil Foden . However, the home side were gifted a lifeline just two minutes later when an unfortunate own goal by Gianluigi Donnarumma reduced the deficit. The comeback hopes were short-lived, as Rayan Cherki struck again in the 59th minute, finding the net with a deflected right-footed shot after a clever pass from Josko Gvardiol . Clinical Finishing Secures the Points As the game entered its final stages, both managers turned to their benches to refresh their lineups. Despite the changes, the momentum remained firmly with the visitors. In the 84th minute, Erling Haaland capitalized on a defensive lapse involving Marc Guehi to score his second of the match with a clinical left-footed strike, following another assist from Phil Foden . With 73% possession and a total command of the pitch, Manchester City cruised through the final minutes to claim a comprehensive victory."
